00:03:54.000 --> 00:04:35.000
and deliver meals to their desks basically? Yeah, initially it started that way and then found a commercial kitchen very, very cheap through a friend who happened to have like at one of those tiny restaurant-like places and then just took a beaten down car to go deliver. And what were these interactions like when you would drop off lunch for people? You were doing this in person at the time. What kind of interactions did you have with people when you dropped off their lunch? So delivery is not just delivery. Like all entrepreneurs,
基本上是把饭菜送到他们的办公桌上？是的，一开始是这样的，后来通过一个朋友，非常非常便宜地找到了一家商业厨房——那个朋友刚好有那种微型餐馆似的地方——然后就开着一辆破旧的汽车去送货。当你给人们送午餐时，这些互动是怎样的？你当时是亲自去做的。当你给人们送午餐时，你和他们有什么样的互动？所以送货不仅仅是送货。就像所有的企业家一样，

8
00:04:35.000 --> 00:05:28.000
right? You have to become a pinch hitter. You have to do everything in the business to start with. But the most important thing is sales. So I would go in and I would be always trying to get more people to sign up. So with the customers who already ordered, I mean, these were people who knew me to begin with, I would just bring in and talk about the day, I'd explain about the food. And I would of course ask them, how was it, you know, as they taste, I would actually wait for a couple of minutes. And then I would always have a follow on ask of some kind, like, can you introduce me to the people in the next floor? And then it became the next building. And I would always bring extra so that I could give it to other people. So in the early stages, it was a mixture of just keeping the current customers engaged,
对吧？你必须成为一个全能替补。一开始，你必须做业务中的所有事情。但最重要的是销售。所以我会进去，并且总是试图争取更多的人来注册。因此，对于那些已经订购的客户——我的意思是，这些一开始就认识我的人——我会顺便进去聊聊当天的近况，我会介绍一下食物。我当然会问他们，味道怎么样，你知道的，当他们品尝时，我实际上会等待几分钟。然后我总是会顺便提出某种后续要求，比如，你能把我介绍给楼下的人吗？然后就成了下一栋楼。而且我总是会多带一些，以便可以送给其他人。所以在早期阶段，这既有维持现有客户参与度的成分，

9
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:51.000
but always pushing for a few more orders. This strategy worked and the business prospered. Saras eventually had enough orders to keep her busy in the kitchen, so she hired a delivery driver. She expected profits to soar, But that is not what happened. Not at all. In fact, the business started going down.
但同时也一直在努力争取更多订单。这个策略奏效了，业务也繁荣起来。萨拉斯最终拥有了足够的订单，让她在厨房里忙个不停，于是她雇了一个送货司机。她预计利润会飙升，但事实并非如此。完全不是。事实上，业务开始走下坡路。

10
00:05:51.000 --> 00:06:12.000
And you actually think... When I say business, I mean literally the number of orders, number of people ordering. Everything was... took a downward turn. And so you start wondering what's going on. Saras wanted to get to the bottom of it. So she went back into the offices where her customers worked and asked them point blank, what gives?
而你实际上认为……当我说业务时，我的意思是字面上的订单数量，订购人数。一切都……走了下坡路。所以你开始琢磨到底是怎么回事。萨拉斯想弄清真相。于是她回到客户工作的办公室，开门见山地问他们，到底怎么回事？

11
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:38.000
So it turned out that, and it was not the easiest thing, and I'm still even today a little, I blush when I talk about this. It turned out that people actually were not thinking that the food is awesome, even though some of them would say the food is awesome. It turns out that there was something about my personality and the way these conversations that we had
结果证明——这并不是最容易做到的事，甚至直到今天我多少还是有点，当我谈到这个时我会脸红。结果证明，人们其实并没有觉得这饭菜有多棒，尽管他们中有些人会说饭菜很棒。事实证明，我的性格以及我们之间的那些对话有些特别之处，

12
00:06:38.000 --> 00:07:09.000
that people missed and they were ordering it partly to see me come deliver. And to this day, I don't know exactly what, but I do know that the initial success of the business was not the food per se, it was the food and delivery combo to put it mildly. And so when you changed the combo and you had somebody else deliver the food, they were still getting their lunch, but they didn't have the interaction, the effervescent interaction that they would have with you.
是人们所怀念的，他们订购部分原因是为了看我来送货。直到今天，我也不知道具体是为什么，但我确实知道，这项业务最初的成功并不是因为食物本身，往轻了说，它是食物和配送的结合体。所以当你改变了这个组合，让别人去送食物时，他们虽然还能吃到午餐，但没有了那种互动，那种与你在一起时才有的充满活力的互动。

13
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:47.000
Yeah, I wasn't thinking effervescent interaction. I was actually crushed that they didn't like my cooking. Ha ha ha ha. So at this point, you've dipped your toe into the world of entrepreneurship. You're starting to get a pretty good idea of what it takes to be successful. You eventually start another business. It's related to drinking water issues in Mumbai. Start by giving me the context. What were these water issues? Yes. So there are thousands of these apartment complexes in Mumbai, three to five stories, sometimes taller.
是的，我当时可没想过什么充满活力的互动。得知他们不喜欢我的烹饪，我其实备受打击。哈哈哈哈。所以在这个时候，你已经涉足了创业的世界。你开始对成功需要什么有了相当不错的概念。你最终又创办了另一家企业。它与孟买的饮用水问题有关。先跟我讲讲背景。这些水问题到底是什么？是的。所以孟买有成千上万个这样的小区，三到五层楼高，有时更高。

14
00:07:47.000 --> 00:08:32.000
And the way water distribution works in Mumbai is basically water comes from the municipality and it fills a tank at the street level or at the bottom floor of the building. And then the apartment complexes have on their own, they have to pump up this water to the top floor or to the terrace where there is a top tank. And from that top tank, water comes into the apartments. And so somebody has to go in and turn the water pump on so that the water can be pumped up from the bottom tack to the top tank. So this was a security guard maybe who worked at the apartment whose job it was to turn on the pump and get the water to be pumped up to the roof?
孟买的水分配方式基本上是，水从市政部门来，注入街道级别或建筑物底层的储水箱。然后小区必须自己把水抽到顶楼或有一个顶部水箱的露台。从那个顶部水箱，水再流入各个公寓。所以必须有人去打开水泵，这样水才能从底部的储水箱抽到顶部的水箱。所以这可能是一个住在小区的保安，他的工作就是打开水泵，把水抽到屋顶？

15
00:08:32.000 --> 00:09:07.000
Yes. And every apartment complex usually has at least one, we used to call them watchman. And because water doesn't flow 24 hours, that's the other issue you have to think about. This water comes in only at certain times of the day. So the problem is the watchmen are not really always there, right? And some of them, they're expected to be awake all night, you know, they've not woken up or they're off somewhere having a smoke or something. And you know, they are not turning the pump on at exactly the time
是的。而且每个小区通常至少有一个，我们过去称他们为看门人。因为水不是24小时供应的，这是你必须考虑的另一个问题。水只在一天中的特定时间来。所以问题是，看门人其实并不总是呆在那里，对吧？而且他们中的一些人，本该整晚保持清醒，你知道的，他们没有醒来，或者走开去抽烟什么的。你知道的，他们并没有在准确的时间打开水泵，

16
